WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.422 --> 00:00:03.105
Unit twenty. First Aid for Bleeding!

2
00:00:04.036 --> 00:00:08.111
Hello, everyone! I'm Doctor Visal, your school doctor.

3
00:00:08.161 --> 00:00:11.317
Hi, Doctor Visal! What do we learn today?

4
00:00:11.367 --> 00:00:15.305
Today we learn about First Aid for Bleeding. Let's go!

5
00:00:16.178 --> 00:00:19.228
Bleeding. Say it with me. Bleeding!

6
00:00:22.709 --> 00:00:25.976
Pressure. Say it with me. Pressure!

7
00:00:29.446 --> 00:00:33.179
Clean cloth. Say it with me. Clean cloth!

8
00:00:36.672 --> 00:00:40.155
Gloves. Say it with me. Gloves!

9
00:00:43.719 --> 00:00:47.069
Elevate. Say it with me. Elevate!

10
00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:53.742
Wound. Say it with me. Wound!

11
00:00:57.196 --> 00:01:00.846
Emergency. Say it with me. Emergency!

12
00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:07.119
Call. Say it with me. Call!

13
00:01:10.633 --> 00:01:20.244
To control bleeding, press firmly on the wound with a clean cloth. Wear gloves if possible. For heavy bleeding, keep pressure on and call for emergency help.

14
00:01:20.294 --> 00:01:23.441
Now I understand. Thank you, Doctor Visal!

15
00:01:25.201 --> 00:01:30.245
Look! What's the word?

16
00:01:30.295 --> 00:01:31.445
Clean cloth!

17
00:01:32.506 --> 00:01:37.699
Look! What's the word?

18
00:01:37.749 --> 00:01:38.899
Emergency!

19
00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:45.250
Did you know? Firm, steady pressure is the most important step in stopping bleeding!

20
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.000
Wow! I did not know that!

21
00:01:47.719 --> 00:01:55.249
Think and answer. What is the first thing to do for heavy bleeding?

22
00:01:55.299 --> 00:01:56.449
Great answer!

23
00:01:57.615 --> 00:02:02.080
Great job today! Stay healthy, and see you next time. Goodbye!

24
00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:04.635
Goodbye, everyone! Stay healthy!

